:true,"_score_rev_volatility":83.4,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.026935420441714014,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":66.3,"_gate_piotroski":6,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":66.7,"_gate_spread":-0.004922660549128231,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.25655512628216826,"_gp_roic_consistency":true,"_score_roic_consistency":57.2,"_gate_incr_roic":0.03113877319461165,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":27.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.007836292921623661,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":30.7,"_gate_pool_share":-0.015343486263682204,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":33.9,"_gate_rev_durability":0.041716133925354226,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":45.9,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.04882177868258172,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":48.8,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.10409291194876041,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.052210092910629724,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.004026124789089059,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":93.3,"_gate_insider_own":0.01011,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":6.7,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"TXNM Energy, Inc., through its subsidiaries, provides electricity and electric services in the United States. The company engages in the generation, transmission, and distribution of electricity for retail electric customers; and owns and leases communications, office and other equipment, office space, vehicles, energy storage facilities, and real estate. It also provides regulated transmission and distribution services in Texas, as well as owns and leases vehicles, service facilities, and office locations throughout its service territory. It serves residential, commercial, and industrial customers and end-users of electricity in New Mexico and Texas. The company was formerly known as PNM Resources, Inc and changed its name to TXNM Energy, Inc. in August 2024. TXNM Energy, Inc. was founded in 1882 and is based in Albuquerque, New Mexico.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Joseph D. Tarry CPA | President, CEO & Director | Age 55 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2017)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $1.2M ranks in the above the sector median among Utilities peers. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["TXNM Energy, Inc. is a mid-cap utilities business with a $6.4B market cap on $2.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 5% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 33%.","The company is burning through $611M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 10.4% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 161% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.6086793703830313},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Regulatory rate-case risk and rising cost of capital \u2014 the allowed return is set by commissions, and the business lives or dies by that negotiation.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Grid modernisation capex burden \u2014 aging infrastructure requires massive reinvestment that regulators may not fully allow into rate base, compressing earned returns.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["30 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Utilities sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Utilities tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Does Strong Earnings Growth Change The Bull Case For TXNM Energy Stock (TXNM)?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/utilities/nyse-txnm/txnm-energy/news/does-strong-earnings-growth-change-the-bull-case-for-txnm-en","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793774381.763,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.917,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"TXNM Energy (TXNM) Stock Looks Overvalued After Its 53% Three Year Run","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/utilities/nyse-txn